### KubernetesManifest <a name="KubernetesManifest" id="aws-cdk-lib.aws_eks.KubernetesManifest"></a>

- *Implements:* github.com/aws/constructs-go/constructs/v10.IConstruct, github.com/aws/constructs-go/constructs/v10.IDependable

Represents a manifest within the Kubernetes system.

Alternatively, you can use \`cluster.addManifest(resource[, resource, ...])\`
to define resources on this cluster.

Applies/deletes the manifest using \`kubectl\`.

