### OpenIdConnectProvider <a name="OpenIdConnectProvider" id="aws-cdk-lib.aws_eks.OpenIdConnectProvider"></a>

- *Implements:* github.com/aws/constructs-go/constructs/v10.IConstruct, github.com/aws/constructs-go/constructs/v10.IDependable, github.com/aws/aws-cdk-go/awscdk/v2.IResource, github.com/aws/aws-cdk-go/awscdk/v2.aws_iam.IOpenIdConnectProvider

IAM OIDC identity providers are entities in IAM that describe an external identity provider (IdP) service that supports the OpenID Connect (OIDC) standard, such as Google or Salesforce.

You use an IAM OIDC identity provider
when you want to establish trust between an OIDC-compatible IdP and your AWS
account.

This implementation has default values for thumbprints and clientIds props
that will be compatible with the eks cluster

> [https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/id_roles_providers_oidc.html](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/id_roles_providers_oidc.html)

